# Antigravity Global Project Rules

Always follow the project architecture standards defined in `.antigravity/skills/`:
- Enforce layer separation using `.antigravity/skills/python-ddd-layers.md`
- Enforce domain encapsulation using `.antigravity/skills/python-oop-rich-domain.md`
- Implement storage and integrations using `.antigravity/skills/python-ports-adapters.md`

When writing or refactoring Python code:
1. Never put ORM models, Pydantic schemas, or framework logic into the `domain/` directory.
2. Ensure all domain entities protect their invariants via methods, not raw attribute mutations.
3. Always write unit tests against domain entities without mocking infrastructure.